<title>USA: Motorola gets $63 mln Brazilian contract.</title>
<headline>Motorola gets $63 mln Brazilian contract.</headline>
<dateline>ARLINGTON HEIGHTS, Ill. 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Motorola Inc's Pan American Wireless Infrastructure Division said Monday it won a $63 million contract to install a cellular telephone network in Brazil.</p>
<p>Telecomunicacoes de Sao Paulo SA (Telesp) will deploy Motorola's Advanced Mobile Phone Service for about 50,000 subscribers in the city of Aracatuba. Commercial service is scheduled to begin in the second quarter.</p>
<p>Telesp said Brazil is the largest cellular market in Latin America and the Caribbean, with more than 1.6 million cellular users.</p>
<p>((-- Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
